  "why": "A part number on ONE side only, bases agreeing: 'The Trial Part 1' against 'The Trial'. The un-numbered title may be any one part or all parts combined -- 'you can't be sure which part' (operator, 2026-09-01) -- so this is neither a match nor a conflict, and it must never reach Accept on the title. Everything else here is identical AND the pair shares an identity Alt ID, which is the point: before 0.26.0 the title scored 1.000 and the Alt-ID bonus could carry the pair over 80. Now the comparator scores 0.70, cmp_titles sets meta part_ambiguous, and the scorer caps at REVIEW_TOP on it. verdict_not_in Accept pins the CAP, which is the part a value could not.",
